    "body": "## Purpose\n\nThis PR originally guarded `extract_required_tool_call_streaming` against an `IndexError` when a single parameter-less tool call closed within one chunk (`'[{\"name\": \"f\"}]'` → `obj[-2]` on a length-1 list).\n\nSince then, #60354 **rewrote** `extract_required_tool_call_streaming` entirely: the `filter_delta_text` / `finishes_previous_tool` / `obj[-2]` step-back is gone, replaced by a prefix-stable span scanner (`_scan_required_tool_calls` + `_RequiredToolCallSpan`). The crash path this PR patched no longer exists, so the original one-line fix is obsolete.\n\nRebased onto current `main`, this PR now carries **only a regression test** that locks in the new implementation's behavior for the single-closed-tool edge case, so a future refactor can't silently reintroduce the crash.\n\n## What the test asserts\n\nFor `'[{\"name\": \"f\"}]'` — a length-1 array whose sole object closes before a `\"parameters\"` key — the call is incomplete (no arguments value has started), so:\n\n- nothing is announced (the span is not `ready`), and\n- the single-element scan does not crash.\n\nBoth the chunked (4-char deltas) and whole-array-in-one-delta paths are checked, mirroring the style of the existing `test_streaming_invalid_name_string_is_never_announced`.\n\n```python\ndef test_streaming_single_closed_tool_without_parameters_is_not_announced():\n    text = '[{\"name\": \"f\"}]'\n    assert _stream_required_tool_calls(text, _fixed_len_deltas(text, 4)) == []\n    assert _stream_required_tool_calls(text, [text]) == []\n```\n\nThis also corrects the original PR's assumption: a parameter-less closed tool call is incomplete per the `tool_choice=\"required\"` schema (each element needs both `name` and `parameters`), so \"announce nothing until parameters appear\" — the behavior #60354 introduced — is the correct outcome, not emitting the bare name.\n\n## Test\n\n`ruff format --check` passes. The rewritten function was exercised directly against both delta patterns to confirm no crash and no spurious emission; a complete call (`[{\"name\": \"f\", \"parameters\": {}}]`) still streams its name as expected.\n\nIf maintainers prefer, I'm happy to close this in favor of #60354 instead — the behavior is already covered there; this only adds an explicit single-element regression guard.\n",
